</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>ACR232:v99#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="ACR232"/><meta name="dc:title" content="ACR &#xA;              232-&#xA;                INTRODUCED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                Assembly Concurrent Resolution
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 232</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Assembly Member Harabedian<br/>(Coauthor: Senator Reyes)<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>August 03, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> Relative to Direct Support Professional Recognition Week. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">ACR 232, as introduced, Harabedian.
                          Direct Support Professional Recognition Week. </span></div><div><span id="digesttext"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">This act would declare the week of September 13 to September 19, 2026, inclusive, as Direct Support Professional Recognition Week in California.</div></span></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span><span id="fiscalcommittee">
      Fiscal Committee:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><span class="Resolution" title="source: /caml:MeasureDoc/caml:Resolution&#xA;    "><span class="Whereas" id="id_52F686A2-E200-412E-B529-EF699A9983B0"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, September 13 to September 19, 2026, is recognized nationwide as Direct Support Professional Recognition Week; and </div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_3827B376-CB7B-48E8-B630-CA993C6D1B61"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The Lanterman Developmental Disabilities Services Act (Lanterman Act) promises Californians with intellectual and developmental disabilities (IDD) the services and supports they need to pursue lives of their own choosing; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_4D06D73E-C278-4CAE-8037-FFA3F632D0C7"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, California is the only state that has established this entitlement for residents with IDD; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_CFB5791B-1B9D-47C9-A7BD-E723D90FCB5D"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The regional center system will serve more than 500,000 Californians with IDD and their families in the coming year; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_813F615E-0E85-43FD-98D0-B227222A2745"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Direct support professionals provide life-changing services and supports to Californians with IDD and their families, becoming integral in their day-to-day lives; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_E9886355-4DEA-4092-AEA3-4B0F1735320B"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Every Californian with IDD deserves to participate as a valued member of their community; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_95A493A3-C866-4EF4-ADF4-22BF68D98855"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Direct support professionals provide essential support that empowers Californians with IDD to live safely in their homes, thrive in their communities, and contribute to local economies; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_F03E1C38-4DE5-445A-BB24-33AF50657E94"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The diverse direct support workforce, with women and people of color at the forefront, ensures culturally responsive services for Californians with IDD and their families across the state; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_71677F0C-389E-4C2B-AF04-68D86EDAF26A"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Through their important work, direct support professionals promote independence and create opportunities that make access and inclusion a reality; now, therefore, be it</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_1C545297-2651-4EA4-8F04-14FD421B8C12"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved by the Assembly of the State of California, the Senate thereof concurring, That the Legislature hereby declares the week of September 13 to September 19, 2026, inclusive, to be Direct Support Professional Recognition Week in California; and be it further </div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_24CEE352-BEAA-4984-B140-DFFDB7C9F37A"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Legislature, having recognized the rights of Californians with IDD through the Lanterman Act, finds that direct support professionals deliver on the state’s promise; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_BED378AA-3A0E-4934-8112-582BB82D0A1F"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Legislature recognizes direct support professionals across the state for their unwavering dedication, expertise, and integrity; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_C8E0BF5B-FAD7-4265-A5CD-067542F72E50"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Legislature honors direct support professionals for building a more inclusive and accessible California; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_799F9C4E-1CDA-4CE7-A060-85CFDF72E3AB"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Legislature is committed to uplifting the direct support workforce and their invaluable contributions to our state; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_B016CD62-0CC6-4066-AEB5-5CB69A162162"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Legislature urges the Congress of the United States to acknowledge the critical importance of skilled supports that direct support professionals provide through home- and community-based services and their invaluable impact on individuals with disabilities, their families, and their communities; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_E88F56E8-20C9-4F19-B974-ED8685FA0E34"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Chief Clerk of the Assembly transmit copies of this resolution to the President of the United States, the Vice President of the United States, the Speaker of the United States House of Representatives, the Majority Leader of the United States Senate, each Senator and Representative from California in the Congress of the United States, and to the author for appropriate distribution.</div></span></span></div></body></html>
